div.p:
Considering that the steamer Haytian Republic
                    wentfrom Miragoâne to Cayes where the same efforts were renewed and always with
                    the consent or the complicity of Captain Compton;

Considering that a blockade was according to law, and that prizes are lawfully
                    made in consequence thereof, and that when a blockade has been preceded by a
                    general notification and a special notification, it is then effective;

Considering that on entering the line of blockade, she there found the Dessalines, which, by customary signals, tried to
                    stop her, and not succeeding, the Dessalines, after
                    firing a blank charge, fired projectiles after her, as was right;

Considering this obstinate refusal contrary to the usages of international law,
                    as well as to the provisions of the treaty concluded in 1864 between Hayti and
                    the United States of America, aggravates the offense of Captain Compton;

Considering that it would not be possible in the absence of papers and precise
                    information on this subject to make a report as to the composition of the cargo
                    after verification;

Considering, in consequence, that this ship causes a loss appreciable in money by
                    reason of the extraordinary expenses that will be necessary to suppress the
                    insurrectionary movement;
